  "plain": "Carlos de Souza is a Brazilian man who says he saw a craft crash near the town of Varginha, Brazil, in January 1996. He says the site was near an army sergeants' school. On the podcast of host Jesse Michels, he says that as he was there, a military convoy came toward his car and soldiers closed off the area. In a later episode of the same show, about famous Brazilian cases, he goes further. He says a soldier stepped back, raised his gun, cocked it, and pointed it at his head. If true, it would mean the army moved fast to seal off the crash and keep witnesses away. Both tellings are Carlos's own, given on two different episodes, and the second adds the threat with the gun."
